                    "prompt": "Draw an original production sprite strip for JAMVERSE '96. Seven separate complete full-body drawings of E. Indigo in ONE horizontal row, arranged 7 columns by1 row, read left-to-right. Do not create extra rows. Each figure is independently articulated, with obvious transparent gaps between neighbors and at least 8% transparent margin at both top and bottom. Figure height should stay below about 78% of the canvas height; keep antlers, flowing hair and bare feet comfortably away from all image borders. Character must face SCREEN-LEFT with body and stride, three-quarter view; never mirror a reference. Use reference image1 as precise face canon, reference image2 only for body scale, outfit, palette and sprite style. Adult male supernatural athlete with azure blue skin, messy icy-white hair, TWO small blue deer antlers, anatomical LEFT sclera black and RIGHT sclera white, both eyes with cyan irises and clearly open; no visor or eye band. Single smoky tilted black orbital ring around mouth/chin BELOW both eyes, exactly like the face reference, never across eyes. Bare upper chest with a clear golden hollow outline heart. Ripped gray jeans, bare feet, no shoes, no armor. Preserve anatomical eye sides even though body faces screen-left; draw the eye geometry anatomically, not by flipping. Empty hands; physics ball added by game. Crisp readable original late-1990s arcade art with bold dark ink lines, consistent face/body/outfit, complete figure. Transparent RGBA only: no checkerboard, no floor, court, shadows, glow, text, labels, numbers, panels, cell lines, logos, ball, or extra props. Exactly seven separate poses in one row. Strip5, seven distinct poses read left to right: run cycle frames9,10,11 (finish a continuous run stride and return toward cycle start); then dribble-run frames1,2,3,4 (forward-leaning low sprint, begin alternating low empty-hand reach; distinct from ordinary run)."
